From 9f64c4624c27b2b8817535be3cd4dfd8d3cb74b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] Privacy and deletion of the account in the app

Stores require apps with accounts to let users ask for the deletion of
their account from within the app. "Privacy and your data" in the
settings has the texts and rules of the web app: what happens (the
follow-ups end at once, the team deletes the account afterwards, records
the law requires are kept), a request only after typing EXCLUIR, the
pending request with the option to withdraw it, and the list of requests
with their status. Downloading the data opens the privacy page of the
website, where the file is downloaded; the app has no file sharing plugin
and this needs none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VRSTuUkoebWWM2DLbPZAvR
